  "prefLabel": "Ban 103.01 Commissioner, Commissioner’s Office",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ban 103.01 Commissioner, Commissioner’s Office.\n\n(a) The department shall be under the direction of the commissioner.\n\n(b) The commissioner shall have general responsibility for the supervision and examination of state banks, trust companies, family trust companies, credit unions, and other entities licensed by the department and as designated by law.\n\n(c) With the exception of the commissioner’s rulemaking powers, and in addition to any delegations described in these rules, the commissioner shall have the authority to delegate within the department the commissioner’s powers, duties, and responsibilities as provided for in RSA 383:7-a.\n\n(d) The commissioner’s office includes the following:\n\n(1) A deputy commissioner pursuant to RSA 383:1; and\n\n(2) Assistants as necessary for general office matters.\n\nSource. #6146, eff 12-22-95; ss by #10258, eff 1-24-13; ss by #14096, eff 10-3-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ban100.html"
